  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider an imaginary ion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><none/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow><mprescripts/><mn>22</mn><mn>48</mn></mmultiscripts></math>.&nbsp;The nucleus contains &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;more neutrons than the number of electrons in the ion. The value of &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&#39; is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>22</mn><mn>48</mn></mmultiscripts><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>In an atomic representation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>Z is atomic number = 22</p><p>A is atomic mass number = 48.</p><p>No. of protons&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn></math></p><p>No. of neutrons&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>26</mn></math></p><p>No. of electrons&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>charge</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of extra neutrons&nbsp;than electrons&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>26</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>%</mo></math></p><p>So, the value of a=4.</p></blockquote>",
